  "body": "This is filed based on a subset of the comments in https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/302#issuecomment-422999075 and is somewhat related to #3994.\r\n\r\nRight now it doesn't appear possible to ask for `TextMetrics` for vertical text, since [CanvasTextDrawingStyles](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#canvastextdrawingstyles) has `direction` but not `writingMode`.\r\n\r\nHowever, it seems like:\r\n* it should be possible to do this at some point in the future\r\n* the naming and definitions of methods and properties should be designed so that extending to vertical text is easy.  (particularly naming, since that's harder to change later)\r\n\r\nSo, in particular, from my comments cited:\r\n> * how do `actualBoundingBoxLeft` and `actualBoundingBoxRight` deal with vertical text?  The names seem like they might be bad for when it's likely to be extended to do handle vertical text in the future, although it could mean what CSS calls \"line left\" and \"line right\".\r\n> * how do the definitions of \"positive numbers\" for all the `*Ascent` and `*Descent` values deal with vertical text?",
